// Readers-disagree.
//
// Two concurrent writes to x, and two readers that see them in opposite orders.
//
// Asserted below, by source:
//   herd7 on the zoo's cat models, run on this program: SC forbids, TSO
//     forbids, Coherence forbids, RC11 forbids, RC17 forbids, OD-LSO forbids.
//   the zoo's equivalence and ordering edges:
//     VbD forbids. Equivalent to SC (zoo edge).
//     x86-TSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     ClightTSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     RC11z forbids. Equivalent to RC11 (zoo edge).
//     CC allows. Causal allows it, and CC is weaker.
//     Slow allows. PRAM allows it, and Slow is weaker.
//     Local allows. Slow allows it, and Local is weaker.
//     RYW allows. PRAM allows it, and RYW is weaker.
//     MR allows. PRAM allows it, and MR is weaker.
//     MW allows. PRAM allows it, and MW is weaker.
//     WFR allows. Causal allows it, and WFR is weaker.
//   the models' definitions:
//     PC forbids. PC adds one order of the writes to each location, shared by
//       every view.
//     PRAM allows. Writes from different processes may be seen in different
//       orders by different processes.
//     Causal allows. The two writes are causally unrelated.
//     POCausal forbids. One arbitration of the two writes, and each reader has
//       seen both before its second load, so one second load returns the write
//       arbitrated first.
//   Not asserted, for want of a verdict to check against: MRD. RA, SRA and WRA
//     are defined on release stores and acquire loads, and this program has
//     other accesses.
x := 0;
{
  x := 1
} ||| {
  x := 2
} ||| {
  r0 := x;
  r1 := x
} ||| {
  r2 := x;
  r3 := x
}
%%
allow (r0 = 1 && r1 = 2 && r2 = 2 && r3 = 1) [CC, PRAM, Causal, Slow, Local,
                                              RYW, MR, MW, WFR]
forbid (r0 = 1 && r1 = 2 && r2 = 2 && r3 = 1) [SC, VbD, TSO, x86-TSO,
                                               ClightTSO, Coherence, RC11,
                                               RC11z, RC17, OD-LSO, PC,
                                               POCausal]
